---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import InterestForm from "../components/InterestForm.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Buying property in Andorra as a non-resident"
  description="Non-resident purchases in Andorra: AGIA agents, foreign-investment authorisation, and the 6%/10% property tax as published by Govern.ad in 2026."
  path="/buying-property"
>
  <section class="page-header">
    <h1>Buying property as a non-resident</h1>
    <p>
      A house is not a residence permit, and a permit is not a right to
      buy. Non-resident purchases sit under foreign-investment rules that
      the Government has tightened.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="prose">
    <div class="notice">
      <p>
        The percentages below are from a
        <a
          href="https://www.govern.ad/ca/w/s-actualitza-el-reglament-de-l-impost-sobre-la-inversio-estrangera-immobiliaria-d-acord-amb-la-nova-llei-de-continuitat-i-consolidacio-de-les-mesures-per-al-creixement-sostenible"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener">Govern.ad news note of 26 February 2026</a
        >
        and Decret 58/2026. Confirm the live test with the Government, a
        notary and an
        <a href="https://www.agia.ad/collegiats" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
          >AGIA</a
        >-registered agent.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>Who typically needs authorisation</h2>
    <p>
      Official Government publications describe prior administrative
      authorisation for foreign investment in real estate. In the
      Government’s own statistical yearbook the cases include a
      non-resident individual who is not Andorran, and a resident who
      cannot show three years of effective and permanent residence within
      the ten years before the application, subject to international
      conventions. Treat that as a map, not the current legal test. The
      operative text is the foreign-investment law and its regulations,
      as applied by the Register of Foreign Investments.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Government has published a
      <a
        href="https://www.govern.ad/ca/w/govern-aprova-un-nou-reglament-inversio-estrangera"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">regulation on foreign investment</a
      >
      giving effect to Law 5/2025, and a later
      <a
        href="https://www.govern.ad/ca/w/s-actualitza-el-reglament-de-l-impost-sobre-la-inversio-estrangera-immobiliaria-d-acord-amb-la-nova-llei-de-continuitat-i-consolidacio-de-les-mesures-per-al-creixement-sostenible"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">update to the foreign-investment property tax</a
      >
      under Law 2/2026. The 26 February 2026 news note states that this
      tax moves from 3% to 6% on a first property, and from 5% to 10% on
      a second home. Decret 58/2026 treats as taxpayers non-residents and
      residents who cannot show three or more years of effective and
      permanent residence in the ten years before the application (study
      absences aside). Read the current regulation for exemptions and the
      10% band.
    </p>
    <p>
      Applications for related company and investment filings are
      described as going through the Government’s service counters or
      <a href="https://www.e-tramits.ad/tramits/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
        >e-tramits.ad</a
      >. A notary formalises a completed purchase.
    </p>

    <h2>Use a licensed agent</h2>
    <p>
      Estate agents must be authorised and listed by
      <a href="https://www.agia.ad/collegiats" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
        >AGIA</a
      >. We list only member firms that publish their own sites, in the
      <a href="/directory">directory</a>.
      This site does not invent houses or prices. See
      <a href="/properties">how we will list homes</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Housing for a residence file</h2>
    <p>
      Immigration pages ask for proof of accommodation: a lease, a title,
      or another accepted certificate. Buying can satisfy that, once the
      investment and the notarial deed are in order. The permit itself is
      still
      <a href="/become-a-resident">an immigration application</a>.
      Parish context:
      <a href="/parishes">the seven parishes</a>.
      Selling later is a plusvàlua and IRPF question. See
      <a href="/tax-residence">tax residence</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <InterestForm
    intro="Leave an email if you are looking at a home and will need a licensed agent or counsel."
    source="buying-property"
  />
</Base>
